## 23. 面试：Encoder-Decoder vs Decoder-Only Pre-Training

可以回答：

> **Encoder-decoder models are naturally trained on conditional generation objectives such as prefix-to-suffix prediction or span corruption, while decoder-only models are naturally suited to full causal language modeling, where each token is predicted from previous tokens.**

---

## 24. 面试：What is full language modeling?

> **Full language modeling factorizes the probability of an entire sequence autoregressively, predicting each token from all previous tokens.**

数学上：

$$
P(x_1,\ldots,x_T)=
\prod_t P(x_t\mid x_{<t})
$$

---

## 25. 面试：Why is causal masking necessary?

> **Causal masking prevents each position from attending to future tokens, so the model can train all positions in parallel without leaking the answers to next-token prediction.**

---

## 26. 面试：Can language model training have more than two stages?

> **Yes. Pre-training and post-training are useful high-level categories, but practical training pipelines can contain multiple stages with different objectives, such as pre-training, adaptation, supervised fine-tuning, preference optimization, and task-specific fine-tuning.**

