# 27. 一句话总结

> **Language-model development is a sequence of design decisions: choose an architecture, choose a pre-training objective, optionally adapt the objective, fine-tune or post-train for desired downstream behavior, and evaluate whether the intended capabilities were actually learned.**

对于这节课最重要的 architecture/objective 对比：

```text
Encoder-Decoder
+
Prefix → Suffix / Span Corruption

vs.

Decoder-Only
+
Full Causal Language Modeling
```

而 Decoder-only full LM 的核心公式就是：

$$
\boxed{
P(x_1,\ldots,x_T)
=
\prod_t
P(x_t\mid x_{<t})
}
$$



# 19. 一句话总结

> **Pre-training uses a scalable prediction objective on massive data to learn broad capabilities; post-training shapes the pretrained model toward desired behavior. For encoder-decoder models, prefix-to-suffix prediction and span corruption construct different input-target pairs, but both can train the decoder using the same token-level cross-entropy loss.**
